      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On October 18, 2017, the FBI raided the wrong house in suburban Atlanta. Offcers meant to execute search and arrest warrants at a suspected gang hideout at 3741 Landau Lane but instead stormed 3756 Denville Trace, a quiet family home occupied by petitioners Hilliard Toi Cliatt, his partner Curtrina Martin, and her 7-year-old son."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8933bf7d996b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "petitioners sued the United States under the Federal Tort Claims Act (FTCA), 28 U. S. C. \u00a7 2671 et seq., seeking damages resulting from the offcers' alleged negligent and intentional actions during the raid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8933bf7d996b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Petitioners' arguments for broader application of the proviso are unpersuasive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8933bf7d996b-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If federal offcers raid the wrong house, causing property damage and assaulting innocent occupants, may the homeowners sue the government for damages?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8933bf7d996b-0000-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government had a winning Supremacy Clause defense. As a result, the Eleventh Circuit concluded, the United States was entitled to summary judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8933bf7d996bc5c2ae8ab08459d4a3adc78f35aa83b11886d7b89cba3e00f97b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8933bf7d996b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Seeking to defend the Eleventh Circuit's view that the proviso applies broadly across all of \u00a7 2680's exceptions, the plaintiffs offer a number of thoughtful arguments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher Mills",
      "case_id": "2024-24-362",
      "confidence": 1.0,
